    "lawCode": "Amd §2.10, CP L",
    "lawSection": "Criminal Procedure Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S3660\n\nSPONSOR: GOUNARDES\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the criminal procedure law, in\nrelation to granting peace officer status to traffic enforcement offi-\ncers and traffic enforcement agents\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo codify the peace officer status of traffic enforcement officers and\ntraffic enforcement agents.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nAmends section 2.10 of the Criminal Procedure Law to grant peace officer\nstatus to traffic enforcement officers and traffic enforcement agents\nemployed by the City of New York.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nCurrently, the traffic enforcement officers and traffic enforcement\nagents employed by the City of New York are not classified as peace\nofficers.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nTraffic enforcement officers and agents are under potential harassment\nand stress at their job at any time due to the actions of many citizens\nwho resent their adherence to traffic rules and regulations.  Many traf-\nfic enforcement officers have been the victims of physical violence for\nsimply doing their job. This bill would recognize the day to day duties\nof traffic enforcement officers and agents with regard to the regular\nissuance of summonses, giving lawful orders to motorists and the special\nduties when assigned to crowd control and enhanced law enforcement\nactivities.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2017-2018: S.5665 - 3rd reading calendar\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the November 1st next succeeding the date\non which it shall have become a law.\n",
